Protection of persons and property;
(d)
Assisting, when necessary the ordinary police in maintaining public order and peace;
(e)
Performing such other duties as may be assigned to them from time to time by the State Government or the
Superintendent;
(f)
To arrest proclaimed offenders and absconders and to produce such arrested persons to the nearest police
station/outpost without delay;
(g)
To give information regarding suspicious and bad characters;
(h)
To render necessary assistance to police in rescue and relief works connected with natural calamities.
